  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing protection of forest elephant populations in key Protected Areas and interzones in the northern TRIDOM landscape, Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) estimation of elephant populations in Boumba-Bek/Nki/Kom National Parks and nearby areas; (2) deployment of camera traps and other technologies to document illegal activities and elephant movement between protected areas; (3) collection of elephant dung for genetic analysis of population relatedness and connectivity; and (4) support for ground patrols and a protected area needs assessment in consultation with park managers.</narrative>
  </description>
